   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to special accidental\ndeath benefits for widows or widowers of certain deputy sheriff members of the\nNew York city sheriff's department",
    "basePrintNo": "S6216",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6216-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 17,
       "fullName": "Iwen Chu",
       "imgName": "1331_Iwen_Chu.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1514,
       "sessionMemberId": 1877,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "CHU"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §208-f, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6216\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to special acci-\ndental death benefits for widows or widowers of certain deputy sheriff\nmembers of the New York city sheriff's department\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill provides special accidental death benefits to the spouses and\nchildren of New York City deputy sheriffs who die as a result of an\naccident sustained during the performance of their duties.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision a of Section 208-f of the General Municipal\nLaw to include spouses and children of New York City deputy sheriffs as\nrecipients of accidental death benefits if the deputy sheriff dies as a\nresult of an accident sustained during the course of their duties.\n\nSection 2 states that none of the provisions of this act shall be\nsubject to the appropriation requirement of Section 25 of the Retirement\nand Social Security Law.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, if a uniformed member of a county sheriff's departments\noutside New York City, or a uniformed member of the New York City Police\nDepartment, Fire Department, Transit Authority Police Department,\nDepartment of Correction, or Department of Sanitation dies as a result\nof an accident sustained in the performance of duty, the deceased\nmember's widow and minor children are eligible to receive a special\naccidental death benefit. This legislation would provide the same bene-\nfit to the surviving spouses and children of New York City deputy sher-\niffs who die as a result of an accident sustained in the performance of\nduty.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nSTATE AND LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
